    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26068" root="ضنأ" body-key="D">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضِنْءٌ</span></b>  <i>Origin, root, race,</i> or <i>stock;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَصْلٌ</span>:
(El-Umawee, S, M, O, K:) and the <i>place in
which a thing originates;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَعْدِنٌ</span>. (ElUmawee, S, O, K.) One says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُلَانٌ فِى ضِنْءِ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صِدْقٍ</span> [<i>Such a one is of an excellent origin</i> or <i>race</i>
or <i>stock</i>], (S, O, L,) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِى ضِنْءِ سَوْءٍ</span> [<i>of a bad
origin</i> &amp;c.]. (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَنْءٌ</span>, in two places.

